## iti112
iti112:1.1 | S: This was said by the Buddha, the Perfected One: that is what I heard. | T: This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard:
iti112:2.1 | S: “Mendicants, the world has been understood by the Realized One; | T: “Monks, the world has been fully awakened to by the Tathāgata.
iti112:2.2 | S: and he is detached from the world. | T: From the world, the Tathāgata is disjoined.
iti112:2.3 | S: The origin of the world has been understood by the Realized One; | T: The origination of the world has been fully awakened to by the Tathāgata.
iti112:2.4 | S: and he has given up the origin of the world. | T: The origination of the world has, by the Tathāgata, been abandoned.
iti112:2.5 | S: The cessation of the world has been understood by the Realized One; | T: The cessation of the world has been fully awakened to by the Tathāgata.
iti112:2.6 | S: and he has realized the cessation of the world. | T: The cessation of the world has, by the Tathāgata, been realized.
iti112:2.7 | S: The practice that leads to the cessation of the world has been understood by the Realized One; | T: The path leading to the cessation of the world has been fully awakened to by the Tathāgata.
iti112:2.8 | S: and he has developed the practice that leads to the cessation of the world. | T: The path leading to the cessation of the world has, by the Tathāgata, been developed.
iti112:3.1 | S: In this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, its gods and humans—whatever is seen, heard, thought, known, attained, sought, and explored by the mind, all that has been understood by the Realized One. | T: “Whatever in this world with its devas, Māras, & Brahmās, in this generation with its contemplatives & brahmans, its royalty & commonfolk, is seen, heard, sensed, cognized, attained, sought after, pondered by the intellect, that has been fully awakened to by the Tathāgata.
iti112:3.2 | S: That’s why he’s called the ‘Realized One’. | T: Thus he is called the Tathāgata.
iti112:4.1 | S: From the night when the Realized One awakens to the supreme perfect awakening until the night he becomes fully extinguished—in the element of extinguishment with no residue—everything he speaks, says, and expresses is real, not otherwise. | T: “From the night the Tathāgata fully awakens to the unsurpassed Right Self-awakening to the night he is totally unbound in the Unbinding property with no fuel remaining, whatever the Tathāgata has said, spoken, explained is just so (tatha) and not otherwise.
iti112:4.2 | S: That’s why he’s called the ‘Realized One’. | T: Thus he is called the Tathāgata.
iti112:5.1 | S: The Realized One does as he says, and says as he does. | T: “The Tathāgata is one who does in line with (tathā) what he teaches, one who teaches in line with what he does.
iti112:5.2 | S: Since this is so, | T: Because he is one who does in line with what he teaches, one who teaches in line with what he does,
iti112:5.3 | S: that’s why he’s called the ‘Realized One’. | T: he is thus called the Tathāgata.
iti112:6.1 | S: In this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, gods and humans—the Realized One is the vanquisher, the unvanquished, the universal seer, the wielder of power. | T: “In this world with its devas, Māras, & Brahmas, in this generation with its contemplatives & brahmans, its royalty & common people, the Tathāgata is the unconquered conqueror, total seer, the wielder of power.
iti112:6.2 | S: That’s why he’s called the ‘Realized One’.” | T: Thus he is called the Tathāgata.”
iti112:6.3 | S: The Buddha spoke this matter. | T: This is the meaning of what the Blessed One said.
iti112:6.4 | S: On this it is said: | T: So with regard to this it was said:
iti112:7.1 | S: “Directly knowing the whole world as it is, | T: Directly knowing all the world,
iti112:7.2 | S: and everything in it, | T: all the world as it really is,
iti112:7.3 | S: he is detached from the whole world, | T: from all the world disjoined,
iti112:7.4 | S: uninvolved with the whole world. | T: in all the world unmatched.
iti112:8.1 | S: That attentive one is the vanquisher of all | T: Conquering all in all ways, enlightened,
iti112:8.2 | S: who is released from all ties. | T: released from all bonds,
iti112:8.3 | S: He has reached ultimate peace: | T: he touches the foremost peace–
iti112:8.4 | S: extinguishment, fearing nothing from any quarter. | T: Unbinding, free from fear.
iti112:9.1 | S: He is the Buddha, with defilements ended, | T: He is free of effluent,
iti112:9.2 | S: untroubled, with doubts cut off. | T: of trouble, awakened, his doubts cut through;
iti112:9.3 | S: He has attained the end of all deeds, | T: has attained the ending of action,
iti112:9.4 | S: freed with the ending of attachments. | T: is released in the destruction of acquisitions.
iti112:10.1 | S: That Blessed One is the Buddha, | T: He is blessed, awakened.
iti112:10.2 | S: he is the supreme lion, | T: He is a lion, unsurpassed.
iti112:10.3 | S: in all the world with its gods, | T: In the world with its devas
iti112:10.4 | S: he turns the divine wheel. | T: he set the Brahma-wheel going.
iti112:11.1 | S: And so those gods and humans, | T: Thus do divine & human beings
iti112:11.2 | S: who have gone to the Buddha for refuge, | T: who have gone to the Buddha for refuge,
iti112:11.3 | S: come together and revere him, | T: gathering, pay homage
iti112:11.4 | S: even the deities revere him: | T: to the great one, thoroughly mature:
iti112:12.1 | S: ‘Tamed, he is the best of tamers, | T: ‘Tamed, he’s the best of those who can be tamed;
iti112:12.2 | S: peaceful, he is the seer among the peaceful, | T: calm, the seer of those who can be calmed;
iti112:12.3 | S: liberated, he is the foremost of liberators, | T: released, supreme among those who can be released;
iti112:12.4 | S: crossed over, he is the most excellent of guides across.’ | T: crossed, the foremost of those who can cross.’
iti112:13.1 | S: And so they revere him, | T: Thus they pay homage
iti112:13.2 | S: great of heart and intrepid. | T: to the great one, thoroughly mature:
iti112:13.3 | S: In the world with its gods, | T: ‘In this world with its devas,
iti112:13.4 | S: he has no rival.” | T: there’s no one to compare with you.’
iti112:14.1 | S: This too is a matter that was spoken by the Blessed One: that is what I heard. | T: This, too, was the meaning of what was said by the Blessed One, so I have heard.
iti112:14.2 | P: Terasamaṁ. | T: (none)
iti112:14.3 | P: Catukkanipāto niṭṭhito. | T: (none)
iti112:15.0 | P: Tassuddānaṁ | T: (none)
iti112:15.1 | P: Brāhmaṇasulabhā jānaṁ, | T: (none)
iti112:15.2 | P: Samaṇasīlā taṇhā brahmā; | T: (none)
iti112:15.3 | P: Bahukārā kuhapurisā, | T: (none)
iti112:15.4 | P: Cara sampannalokena terasāti. | T: (none)
iti112:16.0 | P: Suttasaṅgaho | T: (none)
iti112:16.1 | P: Sattavisekanipātaṁ, | T: (none)
iti112:16.2 | P: Dukkaṁ bāvīsasuttasaṅgahitaṁ; | T: (none)
iti112:16.3 | P: Samapaññāsamathatikaṁ, | T: (none)
iti112:16.4 | P: Terasa catukkañca iti yamidaṁ. | T: (none)

